 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and closed: bodies unexposed behind `(rfl)` `_def`/`_apply` lemmas, no compatibility artifacts or Mathlib name collisions, and all four private helpers mention `derivativeSign`/`thomEncoding`/`PolynomialRolle` so none is general infrastructure in hiding. Both the finite and infinite comparison loops (`exists_*_ne` \u2192 `lt_iff_*` + `*_succ_ne_zero`) are usable without unfolding, and the simp/grind split matches Mathlib's `sign` API.",
